## Chart styling rules (warm neutral theme)

All charts must feel like part of the same deck — same palette, same weight, same quiet confidence.

### Colors

- **Primary data series**: deck accent color (e.g. Terracotta `#B85042`)
- **Secondary data series**: warm gray `#A89F96`
- **Tertiary data series**: light sand `#C8BFB4`
- **Never** use more than 3 series on one chart
- **Never** use colors outside the deck palette on charts
- **Highlight bar/segment**: accent color. All others: warm gray. This draws the eye to the point.
- **Chart background**: transparent (inherits slide background `#FAFAF8`)
- **Gridlines**: `#E0DBD4`, 0.5pt, horizontal only (no vertical gridlines)
- **Axis lines**: `#D6D1C8`, 0.5pt

### Typography on charts

- Axis labels: Calibri 10pt, warm gray `#7A7874`
- Data labels (if shown): Calibri 10pt, warm charcoal `#2C2C2A`
- Chart title: never add a chart title — the slide headline IS the title
- Legend: Calibri 10pt, placed below the chart, not beside it

### What to strip out

Remove all of these — they add visual noise without adding information:
- Chart border / frame
- Background fill on the chart area
- 3D effects of any kind
- Shadow effects
- Gridlines on both axes (horizontal only)
- Chart title (use slide headline instead)
- Excessive data labels (label key points only, not every data point)

---

## Stat callout styling

Use when one number is the entire point of the slide.

**Structure:**
- Big number: Palatino 60–72pt, accent color
- Unit or context label: Calibri 12pt, warm gray, directly below
- One-line supporting statement: Calibri 14pt, warm charcoal, below the label

**Example layout:**
```
        3×
   faster occupancy
Co-working vs. traditional office, Metro Manila 2024
```

**Rules:**
- Center the callout block vertically and horizontally on the slide
- Never put two stat callouts side-by-side on the same slide — that's two slides
- If there are 2–3 related stats, use the "stat row" layout: three callouts in a row, smaller (48pt), all in accent color, with thin warm gray dividers between them

---

## Table styling

Use only when exact numbers matter more than the visual trend.

- Header row: warm cream background `#F2EFE9`, warm charcoal text, Calibri 11pt bold
- Data rows: alternating `#FAFAF8` and `#F2EFE9`
- Row borders: `#D6D1C8`, 0.5pt horizontal only (no vertical cell borders)
- Key cell highlight: accent color background, white text — use for one cell only (the point)
- Font: Calibri 11pt for data, 10pt for footnotes
- Never use more columns than the slide width comfortably holds (max ~6 columns at standard slide size)

