## Data slide QA checklist

Before finalizing any slide with a chart or stat:

- [ ] Headline states the insight, not just the topic
- [ ] Chart type matches what the data is saying (see selection guide)
- [ ] Only accent color + warm neutrals used — no other colors introduced
- [ ] Chart title removed (slide headline does that job)
- [ ] Vertical gridlines removed
- [ ] No 3D effects, shadows, or borders on the chart
- [ ] Data labels shown only on key points (not every point)
- [ ] Legend placed below chart, not beside it
- [ ] All axis labels readable at 10pt
- [ ] Source/footnote added if data is from an external source (Calibri 10pt, warm gray, bottom of slide)
